  "id": "dreamscape-nursery-rhyme-the-family-of-seven",
  "name": "Dreamscape Nursery Rhyme: The Family of Seven",
  "sortId": 27926,
  "sourceUrl": "https://honkai-star-rail.fandom.com/wiki/Dreamscape_Nursery_Rhyme:_The_Family_of_Seven",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-08-16T07:24:06.474Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "text",
      "label": "Text",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Catch a bunch of bad children and lock them in a cage."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Forced into cruel labor, they toil without a wage."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A big hound breaks the cage bars, as cannons set them free."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Butterflies and marigolds eat fruit from the great tree."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Inside a nest they built their own heaven, banded together a family of seven."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-fd2f83423c70d5b9"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In the house are seven people, living in a poor village."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Stonewalled by an overlord, food and drink cruelly pillaged."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Withered trees will bear no fruit, the plants need fertilizer."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Fruits fell spoiled unto the ground, splashed juice upon white mica."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The family ate one of their own, now there's six inside the home."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-a3f4931ab4836f3d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In the house there hid six people, camping in a ruined yard."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Unresponsive sleeps the hound, a broken mirror harms the bird."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Flowers cannot flutter, dead trees cannot be straighter."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The butterfly left home only to meet throngs of cicada."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The big bug scoffed the little bug down. Now there are five left inside the home."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-506422e92cb9e256"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In the house there slept five people, lying all day at home."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "An angel came to visit one night, singing triumphant poems."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Melodic as a dream of plenty both to eat and wear."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Everything is fixed now, closing eyes they have no fear."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Whatever you do, do not awaken — forget those days of past mistaken."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-4727a9bd69884be8"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
